KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ B under construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ after construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Both assertions failed, with out-of-bounds reads: the thunk through which
V's table enters B::g subtracted V's offset in a complete B from `this',
also when the table is installed in a D, where V lies further from B.  The
thunk now reads a vcall offset from the table (Itanium C++ ABI 2.5.3); see
cpp11_virtual_call_through_virtual_base_with_vcall_offsets.
